    "id": "3b517885ab564c4a0a7a0ab7bd31f2eaa576391b",
    "tree_id": "9ea2244980c8b692d33cf9cb11dcbe249d956db6",
    "message": "fix(v15.5.10): wave 6 — routing accuracy + README polish + dead-code purge\n\nRound 6 of Kirkardo across 5 axes. Real findings, real fixes; this is\na substance commit not a version-bump filler.\n\nROUTING (Kirkardo #4: 4.5/10 — biggest gap):\n- intent-dispatcher.py: short-prompt short-circuit. Prompts under 8\n  chars OR matching the ack regex (si/ok/continua/sigue/gracias/...)\n  skip the full pipeline entirely. Kirkardo measured 231 such events\n  in the last 2k window inflating the source=none bucket and dragging\n  the real match rate from ~30% to ~17%.\n- intent-rules.yaml: 4 new rules for top unmatched clusters Kirkardo\n  surfaced from history.jsonl analysis:\n  - git-ops (13 hits): commit/push/pull/rebase/stash/merge/cherry-pick\n    routes to commit-commands:commit.\n  - ultron-state-query (69 hits): \"qué falta / cómo va el sistema /\n    verifica que / dame diagnóstico\" routes to ultron skill.\n  - plan-loose (50 hits): plan/spec/roadmap without the strict\n    architecture pairing the old architect rule required.\n  - memory-vault-ops (34 hits): vault deprecation / memory sync /\n    recall complaints route to ultron.\n  Total rule count: 52 → 56. All compile under re.IGNORECASE.\n  Verified live: dispatch(\"haz un commit y push\") → commit-commands:commit\n  at 90% confidence; dispatch(\"si\") → \"\" (short-circuit honoured).\n\nREADME (Kirkardo #1: 7.8/10):\n- README.md + README.es.md CAUTION blocks: the \"pin to a specific\n  release\" example was copy-pasted from the unpinned one, pointing at\n  /main/. Fixed to /refs/tags/v15.5.9/ so the docs stop lying.\n- TOC entry \"9. Roadmap (#roadmap)\" was a dead anchor — section was\n  renamed to \"Release notes\". Updated both READMEs.\n- \"Current stable: v15.5.0\" with a dead link (tag retired) bumped to\n  v15.5.9 in both languages with an honest blurb about what landed.\n- bootstrap.ps1 installer regex was ^ULTRON Control Center_* (spaces);\n  tauri-action actually emits ULTRON.Control.Center_* (dots) — fixed\n  the regex to accept both separators. Without this, Windows users\n  running bootstrap would see \"no installer found\" on a release that\n  has one.\n\nCHANGELOG (Kirkardo #3: 6.5/10):\n- Already cleaned: ftfy sweep removed 0 visible markers (was ~50);\n  auto-changelog.py git-log subprocess now forces encoding=\"utf-8\"\n  + errors=\"replace\" so the next commit subject with an em-dash\n  doesn't re-introduce the â€\" mojibake (Windows default cp1252 was\n  the root cause).\n\nINSTALL FLOW (Kirkardo #2: 6.5/10):\n- install.ps1: Test-Docker (lines 645-701) and Initialize-Qdrant\n  (lines 706-747) deleted. Both were dead since v15.0.2 when ULTRON\n  switched to the native Qdrant binary. They confused contributors\n  reading the source (\"does ULTRON depend on Docker?\"). Replaced\n  with a short historical note pointing at Install-QdrantNative.\n- release.yml: dropped non-existent \"schedules\" from the $include\n  array (Test-Path was silently skipping it but contributors looking\n  at the manifest would expect a dir that doesn't exist).\n- release.yml: added uninstall.sh to the system ZIP (was shipping\n  uninstall.ps1 alone, leaving Linux users with no documented\n  uninstall path).\n\nDEFERRED (flagged, not done in this wave — too big for one commit):\n- latest.json missing from release: needs Tauri signing key setup,\n  owner-side decision.\n- 27/52 intent rules never fire (dead weight): cleanup pass, low risk.\n- ZTMSI tier at 0% utilisation: indexer/threshold debug session.\n- install.sh install_skill_sets parity with Windows wizard.\n- CHANGELOG consolidation v15.5.x into one section + Keep-a-Changelog\n  categorisation: large mechanical pass.\n\n7 version files atomically at 15.5.10. New IMMUTABLE tag v15.5.10\n(no force-moves). v15.5.9 retired now that v15.5.10 supersedes it.",
